CurioTrail Licence (proposed), version 0.1 draft

Copyright (c) 2026 SG [LICENSOR'S FULL LEGAL NAME OR ENTITY: TO BE
CONFIRMED]. All rights reserved, except as stated below.

"CurioTrail" means the CurioTrail software, quest and lesson content,
interface designs, characters and documentation in this repository and
in the published game, EXCLUDING the Third-Party Material described in
section 6.

1. Free use by individual learners

   Any individual may use the published CurioTrail game free of charge
   for their own personal, non-commercial learning, including at home,
   at school, at university or while studying for work.

2. What needs a commercial licence

   An organisation (including a company, school, training provider,
   charity or public body) needs a separate written commercial licence
   from the Licensor before it:

   a) provides CurioTrail to its staff, students, customers or members
      as part of a course, training programme, product or service;
   b) hosts, embeds or integrates CurioTrail, or any part of it, in its
      own website, platform, learning management system or product;
   c) white-labels, rebrands or resells CurioTrail; or
   d) uses CurioTrail's content or code to create derivative courses,
      products or services.

   An individual teacher or trainer pointing learners to the public
   game at its official address is not covered by section 2 and needs
   no licence. [LEGAL REVIEW: confirm whether this exception is wanted
   and how it should be worded.]

3. Source code

   The source code is made visible for review and transparency. Except
   where a written licence from the Licensor allows it, no one may:

   a) copy, modify, publish, distribute, sublicense or sell the source
      code or the game, in whole or in part;
   b) host a copy of the game or a derivative of it; or
   c) remove or alter the SG · CurioTrail mark, copyright notices or
      third-party notices.

   Personal study of the source code, and contributions submitted back
   to the official repository, are permitted.

4. Names and marks

   This licence grants no right to use the name "CurioTrail" or the
   "SG" mark, except to refer accurately to the original game.
   [LEGAL REVIEW: no trademark has been registered or cleared; see
   docs/IP-OWNERSHIP.md.]

5. Earlier versions

   Versions of CurioTrail published before this licence took effect
   were released under the MIT licence. Anyone who received those
   versions keeps the rights the MIT licence gave them, for those
   versions only. This licence applies to versions published after it
   took effect. [LEGAL REVIEW: confirm the effective date and the first
   commit covered: TO BE SET WHEN PUBLISHED.]

6. Third-party material

   CurioTrail includes third-party software and assets that remain
   under their own licences, listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. That
   includes the island model files (models/island-high.glb and
   models/island-low.glb), which are a derivative of "Viking Island -
   Minecraft" by cubical.xyz and remain licensed under CC-BY-4.0. This
   licence does not apply to Third-Party Material, and nothing in it
   restricts any right that the Third-Party Material's own licence gives.

7. No warranty

   CurioTrail is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
   express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness
   for a particular purpose and non-infringement. To the extent the law
   allows, the Licensor is not liable for any claim, damage or other
   liability arising from CurioTrail or its use.
   [LEGAL REVIEW: confirm wording for the relevant jurisdiction and for
   consumer-protection law.]

8. Termination

   Rights under this licence end automatically if its terms are broken.
   [LEGAL REVIEW: consider a cure period.]

